      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 3,200 mg. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some common regimens you might have meant:\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum for prescription use, for example in inflammatory arthritis.\n- **600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg by mouth, every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day). This is a common analgesic dose.\n- **1,600 mg total per day**, divided into several doses. The order may have meant this total.\n\nTell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do intend 1,600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first, and I can add a note to the order."
      }
