       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, twice the maximum daily dose. I know of no indication that supports it. It carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, and the extra dose adds risk without adding analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit. You also haven't given a clinical rationale.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** Examples are 800 mg by mouth 4 times daily (3,200 mg/day) or 400\u2013600 mg every 6 hours. I can enter any of these right away.\n- **Add a note** to the order, such as \"pharmacy to review,\" if you want it reviewed.\n- **Route the original order through pharmacy or your attending.** If there's an unusual reason for this dose, they can verify it and enter it through the proper override process.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like."
